While this patient has several poor prognostic indicators (male sex, negative symptoms), the question asks which of the listed options is a predictor of a **good** prognosis. The clear, prominent manic episode represents a significant affective component to his illness. In the landscape of psychotic disorders, the presence of these robust mood symptoms is the most favorable prognostic sign among the choices.

